@section 6.4 | Industrial History and Companies

@q 4:87-89

The order is **first cotton mill in Bombay (1854) → first jute mill at Rishra (1855) → TISCO steel (1907-1912) → Indian sugar industry (1930s, with tariff protection)**. The source's key (a) puts sugar first, following its view of the early indigenous sugar mills. **KVIC** (1957) is headquartered in **Mumbai**. **Hindustan Unilever** and GKW are Indian-registered companies with foreign parentage; **Samsung and LG** are foreign multinationals.

@q 4:68

@q 4:95

FMCG goods are everyday packaged items (soaps, food, toiletries); cars and motorcycles are **consumer durables**. **TCS** is India's largest IT company, and **Reliance Industries** tops the Fortune India 500.

@section 6.5 | The Tertiary Sector

@src 5:1
@pyq U.P. U.D.A./L.D.A. (Pre) 2002; U.P.P.C.S. (Mains) 2004; U.P.P.C.S.(Pre) 2003; U.P. Lower Sub. (Pre) 2008; U.P. P.C.S. (Pre) (Re-Exam) 2015; U.P. R.O./A.R.O. (Mains) 2017
In India Tertiary Sector includes :
1. Trade and Transport
2. Finance and Real Estate
3. Forestry and Fishing
Choose the correct answer from the code given below:
Code :
(a) 1 only
(b) 1 and 2 only
(c) 2 and 3 only
(d) 3 only
@ans (b)
@end

@q 5:2-7

@table
Sector | Includes | Share of GVA (2024-25, approx.)
**Primary** | Agriculture, **forestry, fishing**, mining | About 18% (agriculture) + 2% (mining)
**Secondary** | Manufacturing, construction, electricity | About 25-28%
**Tertiary (services)** | **Trade, transport, hotels, finance, real estate, IT, public administration** | About **55%**, the largest
@end

As economies develop, the **services share rises** (Fisher-Clark thesis). **Delhi** has the highest services share of any state economy. **TRAI** (1997) regulates **telecom**. The Economic Survey 2022-23 said **electronics**, not fashion and grocery, will capture much of e-commerce growth, which is why that statement is incorrect.

@trap
**ONGC 1956**; **BSNL 2000, 100% government.** OIL became a **Maharatna in 2024**. **Navratna aluminium = NALCO.** All the named refineries (Digboi, Barauni, Numaligarh, Mathura) are public; **Essar/Nayara** and Reliance are private. **Bhilai-USSR, Rourkela-Germany, Durgapur-UK, Bokaro-USSR.** **UP is the top sugar producer.** **MALCO is at Mettur**, not Chennai. Tertiary sector excludes **forestry and fishing**. **Services = largest share of GDP.** **TRAI = telecom.**
@end

